{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     post.hbs — THE DISPATCHER, not a page.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Ghost renders every post through this one template, so the kind of page
     a post becomes is decided here, by its internal tag. Getting this wrong
     renders every post as the wrong kind of page — which is why it is second
     in abstract/ after the content model itself.

     THE RULE: one branch per collection, each delegating to exactly one
     partial in partials/post/, and NO markup in this file. The moment a
     branch grows its own layout, the two collections that share it start
     drifting.

     ⚠ SKELETON. `article` is the only kind that exists. Each further branch
     arrives with its collection's spec in abstract/collections/, which names
     the tag. Do not invent a tag here.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#post}}
    {{#has tag="#lesson"}}
        {{> "post/lesson"}}
    {{else has tag="#docs-page"}}
        {{> "post/docs"}}
    {{else}}
        {{> "post/article"}}
    {{/has}}
{{/post}}
